(2) PAST THE BIFURCATION AT 1-5 mM?
  constructive (chiral_search.PrebioticNetworkModel, measured S, k_cat, k0; k_homo, rho, phi scanned): max lambda = -1.01e-10 /s (= -phi at the slowest flow; 0 points without a root). Never past: J12 ~ (1 - 1/S) < 0, so no rate factor helps; S would have to exceed 1 (the catalyst would have to make its own hand).
  destructive (Higgs Eq. 5 + measured uncatalysed path), best over the ASSUMED grid. margin =
  J12 J21/(J11 J22), feedback over damping of the (L-D, LL-DD) mode; past the bifurcation iff > 1:
