  Not past at any feed or assumed setting (best at the most irreversible K and R = 1, the grid edges
  that help). The deciding rate is the catalysed breakdown against the uncatalysed one: at 5 mM, s = 6.0,
  the catalysed rate must rise 735x (or the background fall as much); 3658x at 1 mM.
  Eq. 11 alone gives >= 27x (homodimer <= C0/4 = 1.25 mM vs ku/(k2b-3k1b) = 34 mM). The rest:
  a faster catalyst also breaks down more of the fed monomer, so at the critical point free Ala is
  0.1% of the feed and the homodimer that carries the excess only 8% of C0/4. Catalyst
  saturation (SI S4-4) can supply ~1.4-2x. With no uncatalysed path the measured s would suffice (margin > 1).

(3) R9: SLOW RISE OF THE FLOW RATE
  At measured rates lambda < 0 at every flow on the grid: the racemic state is never lost, so there is
  nothing to tip over. R9 not met at measured rates.
  Hypothetical point (catalysed rate x1469, 5 mM, s 6.0, kh 3e-01, R 1, K 1e-06): lower critical flow f_c = 1.47e-09 /s (residence 7860 d).
  static ee at f = f_c(1+d), d = 0.01, 0.02, 0.04, 0.08: 0.037, 0.052, 0.074, 0.103; ee ~ d^0.49 (pitchfork: 0.5)
  started at ee 0.9 just below f_c (f_c/1.05): ends at ee 1.2e-28 (no second stable state)
  slow log-ramp f_c/2 -> 1.5 f_c, feed bias g = 1e-09 (ASSUMED, sets only the delay): ee reaches half
  its branch value at f = 1.44 f_c, ends at 0.221 vs static 0.223; ramping back, ee is gone by f = 0.81 f_c
  -> supercritical pitchfork; the ramp tips over slowly and follows the static branch back and forth (normal form of sim.py / frank.py). R9 would hold IF the rates were high enough.

(4) k2 AND THE 1.8e-6 /M/s FLOOR (R5)
  k2 = k/c as EXPERIMENT.md (k = lambda, c = C0), 1 mM, s = 6.0, best over the grid:
    measured rates:             -1.0e-10 /M/s  (negative: an excess decays; = -f at the slowest flow)
    uncatalysed path removed:    3.4e-08 /M/s  (53x below the floor)
    bound (k2b - 3 k1b)/4:       1.9e-05 /M/s  (needs every monomer in homodimers and no losses;
                                                 range 8.7e-06-2.6e-05; not reachable: the excess lives in
                                                 dimers, which turn over only at the flow rate)
  To reach the 1.8e-6 floor at 1 mM the catalysed rate must rise 4131x.
  k1b + k2b = 1.7e-04 /M/s is a conversion rate (EXPERIMENT.md's 6e-6 - 1e-4 estimate), not k2.
  R5 at measured rates: N.

